# DRY — one helper per rule

A label, glyph, clamp, stamp, fold, or formatter lives in **one** exported function. Callers import it. A second copy in JSX, `monitor`, or another module is a bug waiting to drift.

## Where it lives

Put the helper next to its domain. Do not open a junk-drawer `utils.ts`.

| Kind | Module |
| --- | --- |
| Pulse, age, tokens, tool chips, flow | `pware.oc.core/pware.oc.core.pulse.ts` |
| Boulder / plan / work status | `pware.oc.omo/resolver/pware.oc.omo.resolver.boulder.ts` |
| Path fold, basename, skip, diff stat | `pware.oc.opencode/pware.oc.opencode.files.ts` / `pware.oc.core/pware.oc.core.paths.ts` |
| Row budget, overflow slice | `pware.oc.core/pware.oc.core.layout.ts` |
| `oes.json` clamp / pick | `pware.oc.core/pware.oc.core.oes.ts` |

Two exports that share a rule share an internal (e.g. `formatCoarseSec` behind `formatAge` / `formatDuration` / `formatSpan`). Cross-module reuse is an import: `pware.oc.omo/resolver/pware.oc.omo.resolver.boulder.ts` already uses `toEpochMs` from `pware.oc.core/pware.oc.core.pulse.ts`.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — same fold pasted into JSX and a second file
const label = name.length > 18 ? name.slice(0, 8) + "…" + name.slice(-7) : name

// ✅ GOOD — one export, both panel and tests call it
import { shortMiddle } from "../pware.oc.core/pware.oc.core.pulse.js"
<text>{shortMiddle(name, 18)}</text>
```

## Unit-test friendly

DRY and `try-testable.mdc` are the same shape: extract `fn(input) → output`, export it, hit it from `test/unit/<module>.test.ts`. One implementation, one test file. JSX / `monitor` / `fs.watch` stay thin wrappers.

## Do not

- Copy a helper and tweak one branch — parameterize the original.
- Extract a one-liner used once. DRY starts at the **second** call site.
- Hide a second implementation “just for the TUI”. The panel renders; it does not re-decide.
- Duplicate the “update tests in the same turn” rule — that is `tests-sync.mdc`.
